<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33566" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pamphȳlĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Παμφυλία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a country on the
				sea-coast of Asia Minor</i>, <i>between Lycia and
				Cilicia</i>, Mela, 1, 14; <i><span class="en">Liv. 33,
				41, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 27, 26, § 96</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Div. 1, 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 1, 4, 77</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pam-phȳlĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Pamphylian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">teilus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					8, 249</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 31, 35, § 129</span></i>
			.— In plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pamphȳlii</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				Pamphylians</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1, 15, 25</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
